{
  "id": "queue-kanji-group-not-split",
  "title": "The proportional mix never puts a review inside a kanji group, also across answers (ADR-040)",
  "covers": [
    "queue.kanji_group_not_split"
  ],
  "narrative": [
    "new_per_day is 4. Four review cards are overdue (...10 the most overdue, then ...20, ...30, ...40; graduated with Easy 100, 90, 80 and 70 days before clock_ms, ten days apart so that the fuzzed intervals cannot reorder them). Deckless new cards in creation order: 学校 (card ...50), うっかり (card ...60), then the kanji notes 学 (card ...70) and 校 (card ...80).",
    "Step 0: rule 4 draws the units [学, 校, 学校] and [うっかり] (4 new cards = the goal). Rule 5 mixes units, not cards: R1, the whole group, R2, R3, うっかり, R4. No review falls between 学, 校 and 学校. until_stop is 8.",
    "Step 1 answers R1 Good, step 2 answers 学 Easy. Step 3: the last card introduced today is the kanji 学 and no review was answered since, so the open group [校, 学校] comes first (without the rule the mix would put R2 before it); the rest is the tail of step 0. until_stop is 6.",
    "Step 4 answers 校 Easy. Step 5: 学校 is next, then R2, R3, うっかり, R4. until_stop is 5."
  ],
